## Purpose

Return one static, provider-free R1A oracle candidate
(`governance/compat/fixtures/mfrp_p3_r1a_actual_seam_replay_oracle.json`)
plus this evidence return. The oracle converts the eighteen roadmap replay
families into twenty source-bound normative cases with per-case static
feasibility disposition against current P2 receipt-validation and readout
source. No replay case was executed, no receipt was constructed and passed
to a live seam call, and no observed result exists anywhere in either
artifact. The terminal candidate is `ORACLE_RATIFICATION_CANDIDATE`; only the
independent reviewer may select `ORACLE_RATIFIED_BOUNDED`.

## Target / Source

Target: the exact two-path R1A manifest named in the paired baseline's
Exact R1A Artifact Manifest and the work order's Required Artifact Manifest.
Source authority:
`docs/baselines/CVF_GC018_MFRP_P3_R1A_COMMITTED_ORACLE_RATIFICATION_2026-09-01.md`
and the canonical work order above. Nine pinned sources (seven historical,
two P2 seam files) are the frozen identity inputs; the accepted reconciliation
review is the binding-amendment authority this oracle implements.

## Scope / Methodology

1. Captured `executionBaseHead` via `git rev-parse HEAD` and confirmed a
   clean worktree before authoring.
2. Confirmed the paired GC-018 baseline
   (`docs/baselines/CVF_GC018_MFRP_P3_R1A_COMMITTED_ORACLE_RATIFICATION_2026-09-01.md`,
   SHA-256 `ed0811e913cbd6229aba4fa5662fe0ebf043d79dd02e0002872a932d85066b32`)
   and dispatch base head `6dd4b1e8618257aef872c661eaaaef008b0196d0` are an
   ancestor of `executionBaseHead`.
3. Recomputed all nine pinned source hashes (seven historical, two P2 seam
   files) and independently recomputed the reconciliation review's own hash
   (`8d4d782ac212de13f404021ab4256664696d97321377b1978749a1b08d9ab797`); all
   MATCH.
4. Confirmed both authorized output paths were absent before authoring.
5. Read both P2 seam files in full and the seven historical sources at the
   specific locators cited in the oracle.
6. Ran the pre-implementation autorun gate at the clean execution base.
7. Authored the JSON oracle: twenty cases, one per required roadmap family
   plus two families carrying a second case for redundant zero-tolerance
   coverage, every one of the seven zero-tolerance classes present at least
   once, and every case carrying an honest `feasibilityDisposition`
   determined by direct static inspection of the actual P2 source, never by
   inference from the previously rejected fixture's expected strings.
8. Independently verified every claim before writing it into the JSON: built
   a real canonical positive-control receipt object using
   `_machine_verification_object`/`_machine_verification_digest`, confirmed
   it validates under `_validate_receipt_integrity`, then resolved every
   cited JSON-pointer mutation target against that real payload shape to
   confirm each pointer names an actual present-or-legitimately-absent field
   before recording `STATICALLY_REACHABLE`. No case's feasibility rests on
   an assumption; every `STATICALLY_REACHABLE` route was pointer-resolved
   against a real constructed payload, and every `NOT_REPRESENTABLE_BY_
   CURRENT_P2` disposition names the specific fixed field/sentinel that
   forecloses the family.
9. Ran JSON parse and static reconciliation checks: case count, exact
   family/class set equality, feasibility total reconciliation, forbidden
   observed/actual-key scan, and cross-recomputation of every case's source
   excerpt digest from the live source files.
10. Ran the worker-return fast gate and reran the pre-implementation autorun
    bundle after final edits. The work order's Verification Commands section
    names a `pre-review` phase that the current
    `run_agent_autorun_workflow_gate.py --phase` enum does not accept (valid
    phases are `pre-dispatch`, `pre-implementation`, `pre-closure`,
    `pre-push`); this drift is disclosed rather than silently worked around,
    and `pre-implementation` was rerun as the closest valid, meaningful
    clean-base gate for final evidence.

