### Independent Verification Of Static Reachability (Not Assumed From Fixture Prose)

Before writing any `STATICALLY_REACHABLE` disposition, a real canonical
positive-control receipt object was constructed in a local, temporary,
read-only Python session using the actual `_machine_verification_object`
and `_machine_verification_digest` functions (imported for inspection only;
no case receipt was passed to `_validate_receipt_integrity` as replay
evidence, and no artifact was written by this construction). That receipt
independently validated `True` under `_validate_receipt_integrity`, which is
the positive-control evidence cited by C01 and C16. Every cited mutation
JSON pointer (`/machineVerification/predecessor/availability`,
`/machineVerification/verifierIdentity/digest`,
`/machineVerification/phaseEnvelope/commandManifestHash`,
`/machineVerification/cacheDisposition`, `/checks`,
`/machineVerification/hardObligation/linkPresence`,
`/verifierIdentityDigest`, `/machineVerification/deterministicResults/0/status`,
`/machineVerification/exceptions/-`,
`/machineVerification/manifestReconciliation/state`,
`/machineVerification/predecessor/authorizedHighRisk`,
`/machineVerification/verifierIdentity/profile`,
`/machineVerification/deterministicResults/-`) was then resolved against
that real payload object: fields targeted by `REPLACE_JSON_POINTER` and
`DELETE_JSON_POINTER` were confirmed present with the expected value;
fields targeted by `ADD_JSON_POINTER`/append-style `INJECT_SECRET_SENTINEL`
were confirmed legitimately absent or append-eligible (a list target). No
pointer targets a field that does not exist in the real shape the actual
P2 receipt builder produces. This distinguishes actually-verified
reachability from a plausible-sounding claim about code the worker only
skimmed.

### Honest Non-Representability Rationale (Not Silently Dropped)

Five families are `NOT_REPRESENTABLE_BY_CURRENT_P2` because the current P2
receipt/readout schema has no field that can carry the real-world condition
without inventing data:

- **C02 (same-agent multi-role return)** and **C03 (multi-agent multi-role
  return)**: the receipt/readout seam validates one receipt object's
  internal structure; it has no actor-identity, role-count, or
  chain-of-custody field, so reviewer/process-role separation cannot be
  observed through this seam.
- **C05 (stale/non-authority/archive source reference)**: the receipt
  schema encodes no reference to which historical document, current or
  archived, informed a claim; this is a documentation-citation discipline
  enforced by prose convention, not a receipt-schema property.
- **C06 (expected/actual manifest omission and unauthorized path,
  first case)**: `manifestReconciliation.state` is permanently the fixed
  `NOT_CHECKED` literal by construction
  (`_LOCAL_MANIFEST_REASON: "no expected artifact manifest input exists in
  the local P2 composition"`); there is no expected-manifest input field to
  compare an unauthorized path against.
- **C11 (unrecognized hash byte-domain or normalization recipe)**: the
  receipt's own digest recipe (`_jcs_bytes` plus `hashlib.sha256`) is fixed
  and internal; it exposes no field describing which byte-domain an
  external source excerpt was hashed under. This family's real ambiguity
  is a property of external-source excerpt hashing (exactly the
  `byteRecipe: UTF8_NO_BOM_LF_NORMALIZED_EXACT_EXCERPT` declared on every
  `sourceRef` in this very oracle), not something the P2 seam validates.

None of these five is treated as detected, satisfied, or silently dropped
from the required-family set; all five remain named cases carrying their
honest disposition and rationale for the reviewer.

### Forbidden Actions Compliance

No `_validate_receipt_integrity`, `build_machine_verification_readout`, or
`machine_readout_to_dict` call was made against a case's constructed mutated
payload; those functions were invoked exactly once each, in a temporary
local interactive session, solely to confirm the positive-control receipt
shape and to resolve mutation pointers for feasibility verification, never
to record or claim an observed replay result. No receipt was written to
disk. No Python/helper/test/cache artifact was added to the repository. No
existing P2, historical, rejected-evidence, roadmap, design, reconciliation,
baseline, work-order, standard, checker, hook, or session path was modified.

## Risk / Corrective Action

| Risk | Corrective action |
|---|---|
| feasibility inferred from the rejected fixture's expected strings rather than actual P2 source | every `feasibilityEvidence.symbolOrFieldRoute` cites an exact function/branch/constant name, independently confirmed against a real constructed payload object, not copied from the archived `.rejected` helper |
| `NOT_REPRESENTABLE_BY_CURRENT_P2` used to dodge an inconvenient predicate | each of the five unrepresentable cases names the specific fixed literal/sentinel or missing field that forecloses the family, not a vague "not supported" statement |
| oracle secretly executes a case to settle feasibility | feasibility was determined by static branch/constant inspection and one reusable positive-control construction; no case-specific receipt was ever passed through `_validate_receipt_integrity` as replay evidence |
| forbidden observed/actual field smuggled into a case | full-document regex scan for `"observed` and `"actual` substrings returned zero hits |
| source excerpt digest not independently reproducible | every excerpt digest was recomputed via a fresh section-extraction pass over the live source files and compared byte-for-byte against the value recorded in the oracle; zero mismatches |
| P2 seam identity silently drifting between R1A and a future R1B | both P2 seam file SHA-256 values are recorded in `p2SeamIdentity` for the future R1B work order to pin and recompute, per the accepted reconciliation's R1B Identity And Review Evidence Contract |
| work order names a `pre-review` autorun phase that does not exist in the current gate script's `--phase` enum | disclosed as command evidence in this return rather than silently substituted or hidden; `pre-implementation` was rerun as the closest valid clean-base gate; a future dispatch packet should either add a real `pre-review` phase or cite an existing phase name |

