## Epistemic Process Block

### Expected Result / Prediction

A committed oracle authored by direct static inspection of the actual P2
receipt/readout source, rather than by copying the previously rejected
fixture's expected-string shape, should be able to name a concrete, real,
independently-verifiable field/branch route for every `STATICALLY_REACHABLE`
case and a concrete missing-field rationale for every
`NOT_REPRESENTABLE_BY_CURRENT_P2` case.

### Evidence Comparison

Every `STATICALLY_REACHABLE` case's cited mutation pointer was confirmed to
resolve against a real payload object built from the actual
`_machine_verification_object`/`_machine_verification_digest` functions, and
every cited validator branch (`predecessor.get("availability")`,
`verifier_identity.get("digest")`, `phaseEnvelope` equality,
`cacheDisposition` equality, `checks`/`deterministicResults` length parity,
`hardObligation` exact-dict equality, `manifestReconciliation.state`
equality, `verifierIdentityDigest` presence/shape,
`verifier_identity.get("profile")`) was confirmed present at the cited
symbol by direct grep against
`governance/compat/agent_autorun_machine_verification.py`: disposition
MATCH for every listed branch name. No case's feasibility claim depended on
the rejected fixture's prior expected-string values.

### Contradiction Or Gap Disposition

No contradiction was found between the claimed static routes and the actual
source. The five `NOT_REPRESENTABLE_BY_CURRENT_P2` cases are genuine schema
gaps (actor/role identity, cross-document citation authority, manifest
input, and byte-domain metadata), not contradictions requiring escalation;
they are named honestly rather than smoothed over.

### Claim Update

The evidence supports only `ORACLE_RATIFICATION_CANDIDATE`: a static,
source-bound, feasibility-honest normative oracle exists. It does not
support any claim about what a future R1B replay will observe, whether P2
will satisfy any predicate at runtime, or whether the oracle is free of
defects the reviewer's independent challenge (one changed locator, one
changed P2 field route) has not yet tested.

